      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An acute attack of cephalea and third nerve palsy with pupillary involvement may be caused by a variety of entities, but aneurysm of the posterior communicating artery must certainly be ruled out. We describe a 22 year old patient in whom this clinical profile was an unusual first sign of multiple sclerosis."},
